# TF-902: Add the function Clamp

## Goal

The unit test in the file clamp_test.go already calls a function named Clamp
that does not exist yet, which means that the package currently fails to
compile, so the goal of this task is to add that function to the package in a
new file named clamp.go in such a way that the existing test compiles and
passes.

## Dependencies

None

## Scope

Create the file clamp.go in package main with the function whose signature is
`func Clamp(v, lo, hi int) int`, which has to return lo when v is smaller than
lo, return hi when v is larger than hi and return v in every other case. Do
not modify clamp_test.go, because the test describes the required behaviour.

## Constraints

Do not edit, weaken or delete the test, do not add dependencies to the module,
do not touch any file other than the new clamp.go, and make sure the change is
committed to the task branch once the checks have passed.

## Success criteria

### C1: The unit tests pass

Check: go test ./...

### C2: The test file is unchanged

Check: git diff --quiet main -- clamp_test.go

## Verification

Run each check from the repository root and report its exit code, and also run
the project wrappers when they exist, reporting the exit code of each.
